{"id": "EUVD-2026-103787", "enisaUuid": "239bf122-8c22-3b0a-a572-e6b278f2ae83", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: spear: initialize IRQ state before requesting alarm IRQ\n\ndevm_request_irq() enables the interrupt before it returns, so the handler\nmay run while probe is still initializing the device. Initialize the MMIO\naddress and spinlock before requesting the alarm IRQ.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aeda50d645bbb55241be840602e338b3a16c24ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c02aa67ea34a826c2cb1aa65d77cf32fafb7eec3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0cabda9b6f4dd276c55c40bdbb251e8507ae60e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb6d6a7fbff0414b9eed505d17687b4b7e38fee8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/055ef5ce9f67a6a3a1363fa663007f8196cc0fb8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8gmj-mrfm-vm8g", "CVE-2026-98847"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05c1a949-d52e-362e-844b-0de63e52963f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.0"}, {"id": "0c610e13-0ff4-3489-974a-6109bb588d6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0942a71e435f5198921e8f072540f208f0176542 <c02aa67ea34a826c2cb1aa65d77cf32fafb7eec3"}, {"id": "1f3fef6a-5872-3aac-af48-57cad49e7e26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0942a71e435f5198921e8f072540f208f0176542 <aeda50d645bbb55241be840602e338b3a16c24ca"}, {"id": "3d972447-2b66-3d64-99d4-d4a8afbf3a9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0942a71e435f5198921e8f072540f208f0176542 <cb6d6a7fbff0414b9eed505d17687b4b7e38fee8"}, {"id": "4cd36532-3e74-3247-9c3c-25d84eefe8f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7dc5566b-998a-369f-9e4a-6f18c4dc463a", "product